      "id": "esther:interpretive_note:7",
      "claim": "The book treats Haman's first edict as irretractable and solves the crisis through a second authorization. Achaemenid administration makes rapid multilingual dispatch and sealed delegated authority intelligible, but no evidence establishes an absolute empire-wide rule that every Persian royal decree was legally impossible to revoke.",
